### run 1
=== Is LK memory-bound? N=1, one level, 31x31 window ===

 (a) point count sweep, 640x480 (frame = 37.5 KB at 1 bit)
   points           ms   us per point
       35       0.8497        24.2765
       80       1.7802        22.2529
      140       3.2528        23.2344
      300       7.2875        24.2917
      560      13.7253        24.5095
     1160      29.4824        25.4158

 (b) frame size at 140 points (same compute, wider spread)
        frame   KB @1bit           ms   us per point
      320x240        9.4       3.5913        25.6522
      640x480       37.5       3.2475        23.1967
     1280x960      150.0       3.8091        27.2082
    1920x1440      337.5       3.8223        27.3022

 FLAT us/point => compute-bound, and the 8x footprint buys nothing here.
 RISING => memory-bound, and it should.
